    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present this superbly renovated and ideally located three bedroom, B energy rated home, to the market. No. 5 De Valera Place enjoys a prime position just off Synott Place and adjacent to Dorset Street, placing it within easy reach of every conceivable amenity and within comfortable walking distance of Dublin City Centre.\n\nThis stunning home has been transformed by its current owners to create a modern luxury residence finished to an exceptional standard throughout. Boasting sleek tiled floors across the ground level, the property features a magnificent open plan kitchen/dining/living space designed for contemporary living and entertaining. The bespoke kitchen is both stylish and functional, complemented by high quality finishes and abundant natural light. \n\nExtending to approximately 93 sq.m., the accommodation is thoughtfully laid out and beautifully proportioned. Upstairs, there are three generously sized double bedrooms along with a stylish, fully tiled family bathroom. In addition, the property benefits from a second contemporary bathroom, finished to a high standard, providing excellent convenience for modern family living.\n\nThe property further enjoys a sunny south facing aspect, flooding the interior with natural light and creating a warm and inviting atmosphere throughout.\n\nIdeally situated between the Mater Misericordiae University Hospital and Phibsboro Village, and within walking distance of Dublin City Centre, Temple Street Children's University Hospital, the IFSC, Drumcondra Railway Station and numerous schools, shops and transport links, the location is second to none.\n\nCombining contemporary luxury, thoughtful design and a highly sought after address, this exceptional home is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers.\n\nViewings by appointment with DNG Estate Agents, Phibsboro Tel: (01) 830 0989\n\nLocal agents: Michelle Keeley MIPAV MMCEP, Brian McGee MIPAV, Isabel O'Neill MIPAV, Leah Barry, Vincent Mullen MIPAV & Ciaran Jones MIPAV."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nKitchen/Living/Dining - 7.88m x 4.12m\nStunning open plan space featuring sleek tiled flooring throughout and a contemporary fitted kitchen with modern, streamlined cabinetry and quality finishes. This bright and spacious room is ideal for both everyday living and entertaining, with a striking floating cantilevered stairway creating a real architectural focal point. There is direct access to the rear garden, seamlessly connecting indoor and outdoor living.\n\nLanding 1 - 1.70m x 2.87m\nBright and generously proportioned landing providing access to bedrooms and shower room.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.69m x 4.12m\nLarge double bedroom located to the front of the property, offering excellent natural light and ample space for storage.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.23m x 2.18m\nSpacious double bedroom positioned to the rear, overlooking the garden.\n\nBathroom - 2.16m x 1.84m\nFully tiled contemporary shower room complete with WC, WHB, step in shower and heated towel rail, finished to a modern standard.\n\nLanding 2 - 1.73m x 3.98m\nLarge landing area providing access to Bedroom 3 and main bathroom, with excellent light and additional space.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.71m x 4.12m\nGenerous double bedroom with a modern finish and bright aspect.\n\nShower Room - 2.16m x 1.84m\nLarge, fully tiled bathroom fitted with WC, WHB and shower, stylishly finished and well appointed.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 3 Bed, 2 Bath Home</li><li> BER: B3</li><li> Excellent location</li><li> Beautiful red brick facade</li><li> Cul de sac location</li><li> South facing rear garden</li><li> Gas fired radiator central heating</li><li> Double/Triple glazed windows</li><li> Short walking distance to O'Connell Street, Grafton Street and Henry Street</li><li> 10 minute stroll to the LUAS</li><li> Easy access to Dublin Airport and M50/M1 intersection</ul>"
      },
      {
